::

The surface RELEASES the 880px column (no width attrs on the tab-content). TWO-PLANE MARKUP (WP-N2 stacking on R-C 08-10, AUTHORED this round via G2): the `split-pane` above holds both planes — the roster RAIL as `pane[side=left]` (rows carrying `action=openConversation`, stamped verbatim as `data-action` per G3) and the THREAD as `pane[side=right]` mirroring `thread.surf`: header toolbar, the `::chat-thread` (v0.17 dash-item messages, real bubbles), the gray attach ＋, the composer. The right pane does NOT author a back button — `back-label`/`back-action` on the split-pane make the renderer emit `button.surfdoc-split-back[data-action=backToRoster]` first in the right plane, hidden except the ≤ 767px thread-open state. The shell stamps `data-thread="closed"`; wide AND medium render the planes side by side (rail 280px hugging the nav, thread stretching to the edge with a 10px gutter each side per the mockup), and at ≤ 767px the rail is alone until `openConversation` flips `data-thread=open` (a live-layer duty) and the thread swaps in full-width; the back control closes it. Unread rows render the title bold (`unread=true` attr) with the accent count pill via the `unread-count` attr (v0.17 — the pill replaces the old right-side dot; the count no longer rides meta text) — the accent-left-border unread idiom is BANNED and appears nowhere. Selecting a conversation clears its badge and the nav/tab dot re-derives from the remaining unread rows (it does NOT clear on merely visiting the surface). The Messages sidebar row's unread dot lives in the shell chrome. Roster avatars ride the v0.17 `avatar` attr: circular initials for DMs (`avatar="DP"`), the group glyph for groups (`avatar=group`); the right-side timestamp is the `rtime` meta attr. New Conversation flips the thread pane to compose mode (`thread.surf`) — no sheet. Every roster fetch is workspace-scoped (`?workspace=` required).

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — recorded gaps"]
Split-pane children, the row `action` verb, and the emitted back control are LIVE in the crate (G2/G3) — this file now authors them, and the v0.17 train adds `::chat-thread` bubbles plus the row `avatar`/`rtime`/`unread-count` attrs, all authored above (the bubble-row and meta-text stand-ins are gone). Recorded gaps: `data-ratio` is emitted but has no CSS consumer and `.surfdoc-split-left`/`.surfdoc-split-right` are flex:1, so the 280px rail width stays prose contract, not rendered truth; and `surfdoc-split-back` paints as a text button carrying `back-label`, not the circled chevron of `thread.surf`'s standalone header. `openConversation` still falls to the honest log until the frontend verb round wires the `data-thread` flip.
::
